#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105496 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf98ee24-7774-5674-8a1e-63f4f6d225c0" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "625c532a-d455-5b15-880d-e9fc5ae8ee72" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-374" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\left(\\dfrac 2 x\\right)\\, \\textrm{d} x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $2$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 x\n$$\n\nand get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int(\\frac{2}{x})dx &= 2\\int\\frac{1}{x}dx \\\\\n&= 2\\ln \\mid x \\mid + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105497 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c865ec2-5bed-5892-966b-a586097be923" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating the Sum of a Reciprocal Function and a Power Function"}] :question/id #uuid "9c57c69e-efa2-5e82-992c-53570e61af09" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-375" :question/problem "Find the integral of $\\dfrac 1 {2x} + 3x$ with respect to $x$." :question/worked-solution "Applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int(\\frac{1}{2x} + 3x)dx &= \\int\\frac{1}{2x}dx + \\int3xdx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\int\\frac{1}{x}dx + 3\\intxdx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln \\mid x\\begin{vmatrix}+ 3 \\cdot \\frac{x^{1 + 1}}{1 + 1} + C \\\\ = \\frac{\\ln \\mid x\\end{vmatrix}}{2} + \\frac{3x^{2}}{2} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105498 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df7dddc6-a4fd-5b1b-9b73-8528e5224ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Reciprocal Function and Simplifying the Arbitrary Constant Using the Laws of Logarithms"}] :question/id #uuid "bf47e35e-da86-5f88-b1e7-0cc731c37b31" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-376" :question/problem "What is the antiderivative of $\\dfrac {3+2x} {x}$?" :question/worked-solution "We separate the integrand into the sum of two fractions so that we can simplify each term. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{3 + 2x}{x}dx &= \\int(\\frac{3}{x} + \\frac{2x}{x})dx \\\\\n&= \\int(\\frac{3}{x} + 2)dx \\\\\n&= 3\\int\\frac{1}{x}dx + 2\\intdx \\\\\n&= 3\\ln \\mid x \\mid + 2x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, let's rewrite the constant so that we can combine it with the natural logarithm. For any constant $C$, we can always write $C =3 \\ln K$ where $K$ is some other constant. Doing this allows us to combine the constant with $3\\ln \\mid x \\mid$ term, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{3 + 2x}{x}dx &= 3\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}x & + 2x + C \\\\ = 3\\ln & x\\end{vmatrix}+ 2x + 3\\ln K \\\\\n&= 3\\ln (K \\mid x \\mid) + 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf98ee24-7774-5674-8a1e-63f4f6d225c0" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6838ccf-3010-550f-8b69-92203b5e5c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\ln \\mid x \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104280} {:answer/id #uuid "fbd635a5-cb5f-5860-a9d5-5019c7393431" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (9 - x) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104281} {:answer/id #uuid "3a793066-35ab-5d95-87aa-360459a36f8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (9 + x) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104282} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd150d2-2a54-57e0-bd6f-45a4acd35724" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln \\mid x \\mid + 9x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104283} {:answer/id #uuid "7e18315d-f492-5c27-ab50-67b054520d0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\ln \\mid x \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6838ccf-3010-550f-8b69-92203b5e5c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\ln \\mid x \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104280} :answer-field/id #uuid "042c24f1-4bb1-5ca0-98fa-a8a7455b0d3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104279}] :question/id #uuid "0721a79b-46f6-56dc-93df-e0a639013e16" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-49097" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{dx}{9x}$."}]}
